.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PKCS12_INIT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PKCS12_init ,
.Nm PKCS12_init_ex
.Nd Create a new empty PKCS#12 structure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs12.h
.Ft PKCS12 *
.Fo PKCS12_init
.Fa "int mode"
.Fc
.Ft PKCS12 *
.Fo PKCS12_init_ex
.Fa "int mode"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn PKCS12_init
creates an empty PKCS#12 structure.
Any PKCS#7 authSafes added to this structure are enclosed first within a
single PKCS#7 contentInfo of type
.Fa mode .
Currently the only supported type is
.Sy NID_pkcs7_data .
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_init_ex
creates an empty PKCS#12 structure and assigns the supplied
.Fa ctx
and
.Fa propq
to be used to select algorithm implementations for operations performed
on the
.Vt PKCS12
object.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn PKCS12_init
and
.Fn PKCS12_init_ex
return a valid
.Vt PKCS12
structure or NULL if an error occurred.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr d2i_PKCS12 3 ,
.Xr PKCS12_create 3 ,
.Xr passphrase-encoding 7
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn PKCS12_init_ex
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
